DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     Function ddwwaarrff__hhaassffoorrmm() indicates whether the DWARF attribute denoted by
     argument _a_t_t_r has the attribute form specified by argument _f_o_r_m.  If the
     attribute has the specified form, then argument _r_e_t is set to a non-zero
     value, otherwise it is set to zero.  If argument _e_r_r is non-NULL, it will
     be used to return an error descriptor in case of an error.

     Function ddwwaarrff__wwhhaattffoorrmm() sets the location specified by argument _r_e_t_f_o_r_m
     to the attribute form code for the DWARF attribute referenced by argument
     _a_t_t_r.  If the attribute referenced by argument _a_t_t_r has an indirect form
     attribute, this function will return the final form for the attribute.
     If argument _e_r_r is non-NULL, it will be used to return an error descrip‐
     tor in case of an error.

     Function ddwwaarrff__wwhhaattffoorrmm__ddiirreecctt() sets the location specified by argument
     _r_e_t_f_o_r_m to the attribute form code for the DWARF attribute referenced by
     argument _a_t_t_r.  If the form is an indirect form, the function sets the
     location specified by argument _r_e_t_f_o_r_m to DW_FORM_indirect.  If argument
     _e_r_r is non-NULL, it will be used to return an error descriptor in case of
     an error.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     These functions return DW_DLV_OK on success.  In case of an error, these
     functions return DW_DLV_ERR and set argument _e_r_r.

